Challenges and Solutions

1. High data costs for South African students

Students may not always have affordable or reliable internet access.

Solution:
Noku Ease AI is designed to be lightweight and offline-friendly, using JavaScript without requiring a backend. Students can use CAPACITI WiFi to save articles and resources, then read them offline later.

2. Loadshedding

Power interruptions can make it difficult to complete important work.

Solution:
The app encourages students to prepare their work offline, charge their devices in advance and plan important tasks around available power. It also includes practical reminders such as charging devices at 8 AM.

3. Generic AI does not always understand the South African student experience

Many AI tools provide general advice that may not consider local challenges.

Solution:
I tested three versions of my prompts:

- V1: Generic prompt — about 60% relevant
- V2: Added Johannesburg context — about 80% relevant
- V3: Added full South African context, including CAPACITI, loadshedding, data costs and POPIA — about 95% relevant

I selected V3 because it produced the most useful and relevant results for South African students
